    {
      "id": "fs:860432",
      "title": "Drone Loop – Ambient Background Texture",
      "author": "kkenny101",
      "duration_seconds": 37.3524,
      "preview_url": "https://cdn.freesound.org/previews/860/860432_17997500-hq.mp3",
      "downloads": 345,
      "page_url": "https://freesound.org/people/kkenny101/sounds/860432/",
      "license_url": "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/",
      "license": "CC0-1.0",
      "description": "A slowly evolving ambient drone texture generated with MANTICE by bassimat.\n\nThe original sound was created procedurally with MANTICE and then processed with PaulStretch using small FFT window sizes and a moderate stretch factor of around 5x.\n\nThe processing introduces subtle spectral beating, phase interactions, and evolving frequency movements. These effects add a more organic and imperfect character to the very clean original MANTICE sound, creating a slightly rougher, deeper and more textured ambient atmosphere.\n\nThe result is a continuous drone texture with slowly shifting harmonic details, suitable for ambient music, soundscapes, cinematic backgrounds, meditation, and experimental audio projects.\n\nSource:\nA drone texture generated by MANTICE\nby bassimat\n\nOriginal preset/source:\n<a href=\"https://bassimatte.github.io/mantice/#shared=Photonic_Expanse_20260622_1413a0\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bassimatte.github.io/mantice/#shared=Photonic_Expanse_20260622_1413a0</a>\n\nTools used:\nMANTICE – procedural ambient drone generator\nWeb: <a href=\"https://bassimatte.github.io/mantice/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bassimatte.github.io/mantice/</a>\nGitHub: <a href=\"https://github.com/bassimatte/mantice\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://github.com/bassimatte/mantice</a>\n\nPaulStretch – spectral/time-stretch processing",
      "rating": 4.7,
      "rating_count": 16,
      "provider": "freesound",
